# Supabase project connection — safe to expose to the browser.
# Find these in your Supabase project: Settings -> API.
#
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL is your project's URL (e.g. https://xxxxx.supabase.co)
# VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY is the "anon" / "publishable" public key.
#
# IMPORTANT — these are read at BUILD time, not at runtime. Vite inlines
# every VITE_* variable into the JavaScript bundle when you run
# `npm run build`. If they are missing during the build (for example, not
# configured in Vercel's Project Settings -> Environment Variables), the
# deployed app will not be able to reach Supabase, and adding them later
# has NO effect until you trigger a fresh deploy/rebuild.
#
# NEVER put the service_role / secret key in this file or in any variable
# prefixed with VITE_ — anything with a VITE_ prefix is bundled into the
# client-side JavaScript and shipped to every visitor's browser.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
